{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBBmgUDX9K24xFZvbDZ6Gj","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have now read all the requested files. Here's a comprehensive report on the code patterns used in this Go project for implementing cmd/ utilities:\n\n## Code Patterns in go-unix-utils\n\n### 1. cmd/cat/main.go (Simple cmd Implementation)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/cmd/cat/main.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-219)\n\n**Key Patterns**:\n- **Flag Parsing**: Custom parsing with `parseFlags()` function that handles GNU-style flags (like `-nbs`, `-A`)\n- **File vs Stdin Handling**: Default to stdin (file `\"-\"`) when no arguments provided; explicit handling of stdin vs file paths\n- **SIGPIPE Handler**: Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at program start\n- **Main Loop Structure**: Iterates over files, accumulates state (line numbers, previous blank state), returns exit code 1 on errors\n- **Error Handling**: Catches SIGPIPE specifically and exits 0; uses `formatErr()` for pretty error output\n- **Buffered I/O**: Uses `bufio.Reader` and `bufio.Writer` for efficient processing\n\n### 2. cmd/head/main.go (More Complex cmd Implementation)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/cmd/head/main.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-366)\n\n**Key Patterns**:\n- **Structured Options**: Uses a `struct` (lines 55-59) for parsed options instead of global flags\n- **Sophisticated Flag Parsing**: Separate functions for long flags (`parseLongFlag()`) and short flags (`parseShortFlags()`)\n- **Help/Version Text**: Hardcoded help and version strings with structured display\n- **stdin/File Handling**: Same pattern as cat but with explicit header printing for multi-file input\n- **Mode-Based Processing**: Enum-style constants (countMode, headerMode) for different behaviors\n- **Error Propagation**: Detailed error messages for invalid inputs\n\n### 3. cmd/cat/cat_test.go (Differential Testing Pattern)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-128)\n\n**Key Patterns**:\n- **BuildBinary Setup**: Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the binary once per test file\n- **Reference Binary**: Looks up GNU reference binary with `exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")` and skips if not found\n- **DiffTest Slices**: Defines test cases as `[]testutils.DiffTest` with Name, Args, Stdin, and optional WorkDir\n- **RunDiffTests Call**: Executes all tests with `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n- **Special Test Cases**: \n  - stdin tests (default empty, explicitly \"-\", etc.)\n  - binary data tests (allBytes())\n  - multi-file tests (separate TestDiffFiles function)\n- **Edge Cases**: Tests like SIGPIPE handling, missing files, file handling\n\n### 4. cmd/head/head_test.go (Differential Testing with Normalization)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/cmd/head/head_test.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-296)\n\n**Key Patterns**:\n- **Normalization Functions**: Uses `testutils.NormalizeFunc` to discard stderr with lambda: `func([]byte) []byte { return nil }`\n- **Multiple Test Functions**: Separate functions for different aspects (basic tests, header tests)\n- **Helper Functions**: Uses `writeFixture()`, `bytes512()`, `seq()` for test data generation\n- **Comprehensive Coverage**:\n  - Default behavior (-n 10)\n  - Count variations (-n, -c, negative counts)\n  - stdin and file input\n  - Multi-file with headers (-v, -q, --verbose, --silent)\n  - Error cases (non-existent files)\n  - Edge cases (no trailing newline, count exceeds input)\n- **Comments**: References requirements like \"R4.4\" for traceability\n\n### 5. pkg/testutils/difftest.go (Differential Testing Framework)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-241)\n\n**Key Patterns**:\n- **DiffTest Struct** (lines 46-55):\n  - `Name`: Test case identifier\n  - `Args`: Command line arguments\n  - `Stdin`: Input bytes (nil = EOF immediately, non-nil = provided to stdin)\n  - `Env`: Environment variables (merged with inherited, LC_ALL=C default)\n  - `WorkDir`: Working directory (defaults to TempDir)\n  - `ExitCode`: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n  - `Normalize`: Slice of NormalizeFunc for output transformation\n  - `ExpectedFiles`: Map of file paths to expected contents\n- **NormalizeFunc Type Alias** (lines 27-28): `type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte`\n- **RunDiffTests Function** (lines 83-90):\n  - Signature: `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n  - Runs each test as a named subtest\n  - Executes both binaries with identical inputs\n  - Compares stdout, stderr, and exit code\n- **Built-in Normalizers**: `TimestampNormalizer` for timestamp pattern replacement\n- **Helper**: `ComposeNormalizers()` for combining multiple normalizers\n\n### 6. pkg/testutils/build.go (Binary Building)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/pkg/testutils/build.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-39)\n\n**Key Pattern**:\n- **BuildBinary Function** (lines 16-27):\n  - Signature: `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string`\n  - Takes package directory path (usually \".\")\n  - Returns path to compiled binary\n  - Uses `go build -o <tmpdir>/<packagename>`\n  - Fatal on failure with detailed error output\n  - Binary is placed in TempDir (cleaned up after test)\n\n### 7. pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (Signal Handling)\n**File Path**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5380/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Full Contents** (already provided above, lines 1-25)\n\n**Key Pattern**:\n- **InstallSIGPIPEHandler Function** (lines 17-24):\n  - No parameters, no return value\n  - Creates buffered channel: `make(chan os.Signal, 1)`\n  - Registers SIGPIPE: `signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)`\n  - Goroutine listens and exits with 0: `os.Exit(0)`\n  - Safe to call multiple times\n  - Called at start of main(): `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n\n## Summary of Key Patterns\n\n1. **Flag Parsing**: Custom parsing (not using flag package) with GNU coreutils compatibility\n2. **stdin/File Handling**: Default to stdin, accept \"-\" as stdin, handle files\n3. **SIGPIPE Safety**: Always install handler to exit cleanly when piped\n4. **Options Struct**: Use structs to hold parsed options rather than global variables\n5. **Differential Testing**: Compare Go implementations against GNU reference binaries\n6. **Test Data**: Use helper functions to generate test inputs (seq, allBytes, etc.)\n7. **Normalization**: Strip non-deterministic output (stderr, timestamps) before comparing\n8. **Requirement Tracing**: Comments reference requirements like \"R4.4\" in tests\n9. **Error Handling**: Format errors for stderr without panic, exit with code 1\n10. **Buffered I/O**: Use bufio for efficient line-by-line and byte-by-byte processing"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7572528e-a6da-4fdd-8b4b-68f7c8392313","uuid":"e5fcb035-d45d-4a65-a5c6-06ec73d6e835","timestamp":"2026-05-20T22:52:55.297Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the code patterns used in this Go project for implementing cmd/ utilities. Please find and read:\n\n1. A simple cmd/ implementation (like cmd/head/main.go or cmd/cat/main.go) - read the full file to see how flags are parsed, how stdin vs files are handled, and general structure\n2. A corresponding test file (like cmd/head/head_test.go or cmd/cat/cat_t